WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.710
A teacher showed me a detector’s verdict

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.890
on an essay: ninety per cent AI.

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.910
The pupil had written every word herself,

4
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.530
in English, her second language.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.550
Today: fair assessment

6
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.070
when pupils have AI.

7
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.990
AI-writing detectors don’t find proof.

8
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.150
They guess from patterns, like

9
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.070
simple, predictable wording.

10
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.460
But many people write that way

11
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.380
in a second language.

12
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.160
In a twenty twenty-three Stanford study,

13
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.320
detectors labelled over half the essays by

14
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.220
non-native English writers as AI-written.

15
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.130
A detector is like any alarm: above

16
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.350
some score, it calls the work AI.

17
00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.430
Set it to catch more cheating, and

18
00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.150
it accuses more honest pupils.

19
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.960
A false accusation can hurt

20
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.060
a pupil for years.

21
00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.850
So a detector score is never

22
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.610
proof, and never the judge.

23
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.510
Instead of policing, redesign the

24
00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.350
task so the learning shows.

25
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.830
Ask for the process: a

26
00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.570
plan, drafts and notes.

27
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.260
Add talk: pupils explain their work aloud.

28
00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.490
Make it local and personal, like

29
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.850
interviewing a grandparent.

30
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.940
And do key parts in class, on paper.

31
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.390
Then give each task an AI-use level.

32
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.820
Level zero: no AI.

33
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.580
Level one: AI for ideas only.

34
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.370
Level two: feedback on the

35
00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.370
pupil’s own draft.

36
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.400
Level three: AI allowed,

37
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.280
if pupils show how.

38
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.210
Pupils add a note: which tool, what

39
00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.250
they asked, what they changed.

40
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.860
It’s like “show your working” in maths.

41
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.340
A right answer alone could be copied.

42
00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.910
The working shows what the pupil can

43
00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.270
really do, and where they need help.

44
00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:57.880
Quick check!

45
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.600
A detector says a pupil’s essay

46
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.060
is ninety per cent AI.

47
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.950
What should you do next?

48
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.800
Talk with the pupil about it.

49
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.970
Ask them to explain a paragraph,

50
00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.230
or show notes and drafts.

51
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.460
A second detector is just another guess,

52
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.560
and a zero could punish an honest writer.

53
00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.730
Here’s a redesign.

54
00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.070
Before: “Write an essay on floods”,

55
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.930
which a chatbot does in seconds.

56
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.380
After: interview an elder about local

57
00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.340
floods, draft in class, then explain

58
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.840
one choice to a partner.

59
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.860
AI level one: ideas only.

60
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.390
In the app, you’ll set thresholds for a

61
00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.150
smoke alarm and a spam filter.

62
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.100
Push false alarms to zero, and

63
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.100
most real cases slip through.

64
00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.910
Now picture a detector, where every false

65
00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.490
alarm is an honest pupil accused.

66
00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:55.550
Your turn.

67
00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.380
Mr Okafor sets a take-home

68
00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.060
report on the local market.

69
00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.330
How can he see the learning?

70
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.680
Add a short talk: when pupils

71
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.800
explain, you see the learning.

72
00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.630
Remember: detectors aren’t proof, and they

73
00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.410
flag second-language writers more.

74
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:17.230
Show the process, set an AI level per

75
00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.070
task, and ask how pupils used it.

76
00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.460
Try it in class tomorrow:

77
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.920
“Show your thinking”.

78
00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.780
In pairs, each pupil explains one step of

79
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.740
their homework aloud for two minutes.

80
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.410
The partner asks one question:

81
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.350
why did you do it that way?

82
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.270
Walk round and listen: it tells

83
00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.610
you more than any detector.
